- Rebuilt-vs-SHA256SUMS mismatch and golden mismatch now fail (were
  'diff/cmp ... && echo ok', ignored under set -e: verify.sh ended
  'ВСЁ В ПОРЯДКЕ' with different hashes); bin/* checked against
  bin/SHA256SUMS too (a swapped bin/figram-engine passed before).
- Theorems: all 17 that README/AUDIT call proved (ci/theorems.lean);
  axioms must be within {propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound};
  statements pinned in ci/THEOREMS.expected; Lean sources scanned for
  axiom/native_decide/implemented_by/extern/sorry/admit/skipKernelTC.
- Coverage must be complete; counts parsed and required non-zero / at
  floors; lax-parser control must fail because of mismatches, not a crash;
  C compiler diagnostics kept; Go mandatory (FIGRAM_WAIVE=go -> exit 3);
  race test must actually run (--- PASS line); protocol_edges.py step.
- Exit codes: 0 full pass, 1 failure, 3 passed with declared deviations
  (FIGRAM_SHA256SUMS for another toolchain, FIGRAM_WAIVE=go).
- Prints provenance (commit, dirty count, script hash, tool versions).

Integration note: verify.sh conflict resolved on top of harness-ci's version.
Kept from the integration branch: the strict proof gate step (proofs 90201dd; both gates
run: ci/theorems.lean pins pp-statements of 17 README/AUDIT theorems and bans
implemented_by/@[extern]; strict_gate.sh covers all 79 source theorems, the environment
and leanchecker), client_robustness.py (python-client 1df3ef8), and the ffi-go Bot
regression tests next to TestSharedRequestMap (each must print --- PASS). Expectations
updated to the integrated tools' outputs: json_fuzz now also reports records Figram
cannot re-read (177355a, must be 0), host_sim reports per-user outcomes (c8bb903/1dfe574)
and control attempts (253df6b); the same two expectations fixed in verify-prebuilt.sh.

